%I A400594 #13 Oct 13 2026 18:17:53
%S A400594 2,2,3,5,8,13,22,38,65,112,192
%N A400594 Maximum number of items among which exactly two defectives can always be identified in at most n adaptive tests, each returning the number of defectives in a selected subset.
%H A400594 Fedor Karpelevitch, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.38489">Certified exact bounds for adaptive quantitative group testing with two defectives</a>, arXiv:2609.38489 [math.CO], 2026.
%H A400594 Fedor Karpelevitch, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23006289">Reproduction materials for certified exact bounds in two-defective quantitative group testing</a>, version 1.0.0, 2026.
%F A400594 a(n) <= floor((1 + sqrt(1 + 8*3^n))/2).
%F A400594 a(n+1) <= 2*a(n).
%F A400594 a(11) >= 328.
%e A400594 For n = 3, a(3) = 5: for items 1..5, test {1,2}. After result 0, test {3}, then {4}. After result 1, test {1,3}, then {4} after 0 or {1,4} after 1.
%Y A400594 Cf. A000079, A000225, A000325, A132824, A400595.
%Y A400594 Cf. A400600.
%K A400594 nonn,hard,more,new
%O A400594 0,1
%A A400594 _Fedor Karpelevitch_, Sep 30 2026
